# Cloudflare Workers static assets deploy scans the whole "." directory by
# default -- this excludes everything that isn't actually the live static
# site, so it doesn't choke on huge/irrelevant files (this is what caused
# the "Asset too large" .git pack-file error).

# Not deployed to Cloudflare at all -- this runs on Vercel as a Python function.
backend/

# Stale duplicate from an old Railway deployment attempt -- not the live site.
frontend/

# Rust build cache + unused sibling project (137MB+ of build artifacts).
wasm-model-parser/
rust-model-parser/

# Git internals -- this is what triggered the original 57.5MB pack-file error.
.git/

# Worker source/config -- these run the site, they shouldn't also be served
# as downloadable static files.
worker.js
wrangler.jsonc

# Misc non-site files.
*.zip
NEW BANNER V5.gif
README.md
CREDITS.md
LICENSE
railway.toml
Procfile
vercel.json
.vercelignore
